---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
const email = "hello@bosskg.com";
const updated = "August 18, 2026";
---
<Base title="Editorial Standards — BOSS KG" description="How BOSS KG researches, writes, sources and corrects its coverage.">
  <main class="wrap">
    <article class="article">
      <div class="a-head"><h1>Editorial Standards</h1></div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p><em>Last updated: {updated}</em></p>
        <p>
          BOSS KG covers Marvel games, the MCU and gaming news for fans. These standards explain
          how we work so you know what to expect from our coverage.
        </p>

        <h2>Independence</h2>
        <p>
          We are an independent, fan-run brand. We are not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
          sponsored by any publisher, studio or platform we cover. Sponsored content, when it
          appears, is clearly labelled.
        </p>

        <h2>Sourcing &amp; attribution</h2>
        <p>
          Our news posts are original write-ups of developments reported across the industry. When
          a story originates with another outlet or an official source, we credit and link to it so
          you can read the original reporting. We distinguish confirmed news from rumours and
          speculation, and we label rumours as such.
        </p>

        <h2>Accuracy &amp; corrections</h2>
        <p>
          We aim to be accurate and fair. When we get something wrong, we fix it and note
          significant corrections. Spotted an error? Email
          <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> with the headline and the correction.
        </p>

        <h2>Imagery</h2>
        <p>
          Game and film imagery, screenshots, key art and trademarks belong to their respective
          owners and are used for editorial identification and commentary. We do not claim
          ownership of these materials.
        </p>

        <h2>AI &amp; production</h2>
        <p>
          We may use tools to help research, draft and produce coverage, but editorial decisions
          and this Site's standards are ours. We do not publish fabricated quotes or events.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about our standards? Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</Base>
